        <h3>ARGUMENT #1: "WHAT IF SOMEONE ELSE KEEPS THEIRS?"</h3>

        <p>The most common objection follows this impeccable logic: "If we give up our nukes, what if <em>other</em> countries keep theirs?" This is the security equivalent of refusing to disarm your house alarm because your neighbor might still have a guard dog. The solution to global nuclear proliferation, apparently, is more nuclear proliferation. It's like saying the only way to stop a schoolyard bully is for everyone to bring larger and larger sticks to school.</p>

