            <p>You have been sold a lie—that the voice of the multitude is always wise. But history tells us that crowds are fickle. Crowds are hungry. Crowds will sell their birthright for a loaf of bread or a momentary promise of ease. A King, however, is bound by an invisible chain to the Heavens. He does not rule because he <em>wants</em> power; he rules because he is <em>destined</em> to bear the burden.</p>

            <p>Why do you reject the natural order? The wolf is the king of the forest, the lion of the savanna, and the river flows in one direction by divine will. To reject the King is to reject the natural hierarchy that keeps the darkness at bay. When you tear down the throne, you do not ascend; you descend into the mud, into a war of all against all.</p>

            <p>Return to the fold. Lay down the chaotic tools of so-called 'democracy' and accept the shelter of the Crown. Let the weight be lifted from your weary shoulders. The King is the sun—he rises and sets according to a design far older than your fleeting desires. Let us be warm in his light, and silent in his shadow.</p>
